==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Chilopod_%28Marshal_Hedin%29.jpg|thumb|right|A '''centipede'''.]]
{{wikispecies|Chilopoda}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*ped-}}
From {{uder|en|fr|centipède}}, from {{der|en|la|centipeda}}, {{m|la|centipēs}}, from {{m|la|centi-||hundred}} + {{m|la|pēs||foot}};<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n}}</ref><ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary|pos=n}}</ref> equivalent to {{confix|en|centi<id:hundred>|pede}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɛn.tɪ.pid/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-centipede.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q43447}}Any [[arthropod]] of class {{taxfmt|Chilopoda|class}}, which have a [[segmented]] body with one pair of legs per segment and from about 20 to 300 legs in total.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1993|author=Gordon M. Nishida; JoAnn M. Tenorio|title=What Bit Me?: Identifying Hawai'i's Stinging and Biting Insects and Their Kin|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=a-TnX5GLiT4C&pg=PA29&dq=%22centipede%22%7C%22centipedes%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=ypOMU_--JMW6kAWLtYCoBg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22centipede%22%7C%22centipedes%22&f=false|page=29
|passage='''Centipedes''' differ from millipedes by having a single pair of legs on each body segment.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=Thom Holmes|title=March Onto Land: The Silurian Period to the Middle Triassic Epoch|page=58|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=j-sOYynMAAMC&pg=PA58&dq=%22centipede%22%7C%22centipedes%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=ypOMU_--JMW6kAWLtYCoBg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22centipede%22%7C%22centipedes%22&f=false|passage=The existence of millipedes, '''centipedes''', insects, and spiders along-side the first tetrapods sustained a robust ecosystem in which most animals were predators or scavengers.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Alan Gunn|title=Essential Forensic Biology|edition=2nd|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=IaQsqg7bKS0C&pg=PT94&dq=%22centipede%22%7C%22centipedes%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=ypOMU_--JMW6kAWLtYCoBg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22centipede%22%7C%22centipedes%22&f=false|page=unnumbered
|passage=All '''centipedes''' (Chilopoda) and spiders (Aranea) are predatory and although they are often found on corpses their impact on the other fauna is not known.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A many-[[oared]] [[Chinese]] [[smuggling]] [[boat]].
#: {{syn|en|fast crab|scrambling dragon}}

====Usage notes====
* The spelling "[[centiped]]" was formerly considered the only correct form by [[prescriptivist]]s and is still preferred by many scientists who work with [[myriapod]]s, but this spelling is by far the most common in actual use.

